  "id": "COMPOUND:24046 - PROTEIN:5777",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex network of interactions between Anguidine deriv scirpentriol and SF-188, mediated through multiple targets. The drug, Anguidine deriv scirpentriol, is implicated in targeting Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which in turn is a target of 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, and ultimately SF-188. Additionally, Anguidine deriv scirpentriol is also shown to target Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which is a target of Magnocurarine, and this same Thioredoxin, mitochondrial is also a target of another compound, 10,13-dimethyl-17-(5-propan-2-ylhept-5-en-2-yl)-2,3,4,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-dodecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-ol, which also targets SF-188. These findings collectively indicate that Anguidine deriv scirpentriol may exert its biological effects through multiple pathways, with SF-188 being a downstream target in several of these pathways. The evidence supports a potential role for Anguidine deriv scirpentriol in modulating SF-188 activity, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
